            "text": "leaf spine"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " chain. Stitch heights increase from dc to htr to tr at the widest point, then decrease back to the tip using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "leaf-shaping"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "leaf shaping"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The result is a pointed oval that lies flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make ten leaves in each of two greens. Thread onto jute twine through the base loop. Total yarn around 100 m."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
